From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shphadnis <134159681+shphadnis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:09:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] spectro: let virt-v2v copy vSphere disks when no VDDK image
 is set

Patch 0002 made CDI+VDDK the only transfer path for vSphere, so a provider
without a VDDK image could not migrate at all. Restore upstream's virt-v2v
transfer for that case, keeping CDI+VDDK whenever an image is configured:

- ShouldUseV2vForTransfer returns false for vSphere only when a VDDK image
  is set (provider vddkInitImage, else the controller's VDDK_IMAGE). Without
  one, upstream's rules apply: a cold migration to the host cluster has
  virt-v2v copy and convert the disks (nbdkit over HTTPS through vCenter);
  warm, remote-destination, shared-disk, excludeDisks, NetApp shift and
  offload plans keep the CDI path.
- vSphere DataVolumes() gets upstream's Blank source back for that path.
- Conversion is opt-in on this fork and the virt-v2v copy runs as part of
  conversion, so plan validation now rejects a vSphere plan with no VDDK
  image unless the provider sets convertDisk: true. Without that the copy
  phase is skipped and the VM would get empty disks.

plan_transfer_test.go goes back to upstream's assertions (with VDDK_IMAGE
cleared) and the guard test now pins both sides of the VDDK switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
